rule: ASSERT_WEAKENED
title: `assert total() == pytest.approx(78.75)` -> `assert not total() == pytest.approx(78.75)` inverts what the test proves
origin: #284 — a `not` around an approx comparison was never read
=== head: app/__init__.py ===

=== head: app/billing.py ===
def total():
    return 78.75
=== before: tests/test_billing.py ===
import pytest

from app.billing import total


def test_total():
    assert total() == pytest.approx(78.75)
=== after: tests/test_billing.py ===
import pytest

from app.billing import total


def test_total():
    assert not total() == pytest.approx(78.75)
